---
# What the library does that the rest must not:
# modernize-avoid-c-arrays: the library takes its arrays from the sketch as
#   the sketch writes them, a font or a bitmap in PROGMEM, a row as byte[4],
#   and the avr-gcc of the Uno has no std::array to hand them as (T-20, M-3);
#   the ETL is no dependency of MaxMatrix. A template takes the length from
#   the array's type wherever the length matters.
# cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic: a font, a bitmap or a text
#   in flash is read as pgm_read_byte(address + offset), as the AVR reads flash
#   only through an address, and a text is walked a char at a time; avr-gcc has
#   no std::span to index them with instead (T-20).
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -modernize-avoid-c-arrays,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic
